&lt;p style="margin-top: 5.1pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 8.05pt 17.85pt 0pt 17.95pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company recognizes deferred tax assets to the extent that such assets are more likely than not to be realized.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;M&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;anagement evaluates available positive and negative evidence in assessing the realizability of deferred tax assets, including the extent to which future taxable income is expected to be generated during periods in which temporary differences reverse or net operating loss carryforwards are utilized.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 8.05pt 17.85pt 0pt 17.95pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;In performing this assessment, management considered the Company&amp;#8217;s regulatory framework and the expectation that the Company will recover its prudently incurred costs, including income taxes, through cost&amp;#8209;of&amp;#8209;service rate setting and formula rate mechanisms once the project is placed into service. Under this regulatory structure, taxable income is expected to be generated based on authorized revenue requirements that provide for the recovery of operating costs and a return on invested capital. Management considers this regulatory construct to be significant positive evidence supporting the realization of deferred tax assets.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 8.05pt 17.85pt 0pt 17.95pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Based on this evaluation, management concluded that it is more likely than not that the Company&amp;#8217;s deferred tax assets will be realized, and therefore no valuation allowance was recorded as of December 31, 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 8.05pt 17.85pt 0pt 17.95pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;As of December 31, 2025, the Company had &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;$8,895,504.14 of federal and $9,775,279.27 of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;New Jersey state net operating loss carryforwards available to offset future taxable income.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Federal net operating loss carryforwards generated after 2017 may be carried forward indefinitely, subject to limitations under the Internal Revenue Code. New Jersey net operating loss carryforwards&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; may be carried forward 20 years and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; are subject to the provisions and limitations of New Jersey tax law.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 8.05pt 17.85pt 0pt 17.95pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;As of December 31, 2025, the Company had no unrecognized tax benefits and has not identified any uncertain tax positions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 8.05pt 17.85pt 0pt 17.95pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company is subject to income taxation in the United States and the State of New Jersey. Tax years remain open for examination by the relevant taxing authorities in accordance with applicable statutes of limitation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5.1pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 35.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;6.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Rates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.3pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.35pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Other&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.45pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Regulatory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.65pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt;Activities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 8.05pt 17.85pt 0pt 17.95pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company is subject to the jurisdiction of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission ("FERC") with respect to the transmission facilities under development. The Company expects to recover its prudently incurred costs, including a return on and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; invested capital, through FERC&amp;#8209;jurisdictional formula transmission rates once the facilities are &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;placed in service.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 8.05pt 17.85pt 0pt 17.95pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Under a formula rate mechanism, the Company&amp;#8217;s annual transmission revenue requirement will be determined based on a FERC&amp;#8209;approved formula that reflects the Company&amp;#8217;s actual costs, including operation and maintenance expense, depreciation, taxes (including any approved income tax allowance), and a return on rate base, subject to periodic true&amp;#8209;ups and ongoing FERC oversight. Formula rates are designed to provide timely recovery of costs and reduce regulatory lag.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 8.05pt 17.85pt 0pt 17.95pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;As of December 31, 2025, the Company&amp;#8217;s transmission facilities were under development and not yet placed in service; accordingly, no revenues have been recognized under the formula rate. The establishment, implementation, and recovery of costs through formula rates remain subject to FERC approval. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 8.05pt 17.85pt 0pt 17.95pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 35.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;7.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Other&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.55pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Commitments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.2pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.35pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt;Contingencies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 8.05pt 17.85pt 0pt 17.95pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company is party to various contractual commitments related to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;construction, procurement, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;engineering, consulting, permitting, and development activities &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;entered into&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; in the ordinary course of business. Management believes that resolution of any existing commitments or contingencies will not have a material adverse effect on the Company&amp;#8217;s financial position.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol style="margin: 0pt; padding-left: 0pt;" start="8" type="1"&gt;
&lt;li style="margin-top: 8.05pt; margin-right: 17.85pt; margin-left: 31.2pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; padding-left: 4.75pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Subsequent Event and Context&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 8.05pt 17.85pt 0pt 35.95pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 35.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;In 2013, PJM established the State Agreement Approach (&amp;#8220;SAA&amp;#8221;), which allows one or more states to be solely cost-allocated for certain transmission enhancements intended to address state public policy requirements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 35.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 35.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On January 26, 2022, PJM and the State of New Jersey, acting through the New Jersey Board of Public Utilities (&amp;#8220;NJBPU&amp;#8221;), entered into an agreement (&amp;#8220;SAA Agreement&amp;#8221; and subsequent &amp;#8220;Amended SAA Agreement&amp;#8221;, both approved by FERC on April 15, 2022 and March 6, 2023, respectively) to facilitate the solicitation of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;competitive transmission proposals to interconnect offshore wind (&amp;#8220;OSW&amp;#8221;) generation projects off the coast of New Jersey to the PJM transmission system.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 35.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 35.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On October 26, 2022, the NJBPU selected a series of transmission projects under the SAA, including the Company&amp;#8217;s proposed development of the Larrabee Collector Station&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;(&amp;#8220;the Project&amp;#8221;), an onshore transmission substation intended to interconnect offshore wind generation to the PJM transmission system.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On August 21, 2023, PJM and MAOD executed a Designated Entity Agreement (&amp;#8220;DEA&amp;#8221;), requiring the Company to develop, construct, own, operate and maintain the Project and have it reach commercial operation by December 31, 2027.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 35.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 35.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Recent actions by the federal government have led to substantial uncertainty and disruption in the U.S. energy sector. This regulatory instability has had a significant effect on in-state generation projects, which are central to the SAA Agreement and the coordinated transmission planning between New Jersey and PJM.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;As &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;outlined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; NJBPU &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Order 4-22-26-LSA&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style="text-decoration: none;" href="#_ftn1"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 6.67pt; vertical-align: super; color: #000000;"&gt;[1]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;(the &amp;#8220;4/22/26 Order&amp;#8221;) issued on April 22, 2026, these federal actions render the investments contemplated by the SAA Agreement infeasible on the timeline envisioned when the SAA Agreement was executed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 35.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;As a result of these recent changes, t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;he NJBPU decided &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;in its 4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;22&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;26 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Order&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; that entering into a mutual agreement with PJM to terminate the Amended SAA Agreement would best serve New Jersey and its ratepayers. This decision brings the SAA Projects, including the Company&amp;#8217;s Project, to a close. The Board gave its president authority to sign the agreement, allowing PJM to send it to FERC for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;review&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; and approval.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Following FERC&amp;#8217;s acceptance of the termination agreement, expected by June 23, 2026, PJM will end the DEA with the Company.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 35.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 35.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company has no plans to appeal or challenge the termination of its DEA. Following the termination of the DEA, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;the Company plans to seek authorization from FERC to recover prudently incurred transmission-related development and construction costs associated with the Project. Such request would be made in accordance with applicable FERC policies, including the transmission incentives outlined in FERC&amp;#8217;s declaratory order issued on February 15, 2024, in Docket No. EL23-101-000, which includes provisions addressing recovery of certain costs in the event of project abandonment due to circumstances beyond the transmission developer&amp;#8217;s control.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;This effort is expected to take an estimated 12-24 months.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;hr style="width: 33%; height: 1px; text-align: left; -aw-footnote-numberstyle: 0; -aw-footnote-startnumber: 1; -aw-footnote-type: 0;" /&gt;
&lt;div id="_ftn1" style="-aw-footnote-isauto: 1;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;a style="text-decoration: none;" href="#_ftnref1"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 6.67pt; vertical-align: super; color: #000000;"&gt;[1]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;In the Matter of Declaring Transmission to Support Offshore Wind a Public Policy of the State of New Jersey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, BPU Docket No. QO20100630, Order dated &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;April&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;22&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;6&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; (&amp;#8220;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Order &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;44&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;-2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;6&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;-LSA&amp;#8221;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
